    keys: ['enamel', 'dentin', 'pulp', 'cementum', 'layer', 'layers'],
    en: 'Enamel is the hard outer shell. It has no feeling. Under it, dentin is softer and can feel cold and sweet. The pulp in the center has the nerve and blood supply. That is the part a root canal treats. Cementum covers the root. Once enamel is scratched or dissolved away, the body does not grow a new layer, which is why acid, grinding, and hard scrubs matter.',
    tl: 'Ang enamel ay matigas na panlabas na balat. Wala itong pakiramdam. Sa ilalim nito, mas malambot ang dentin at doon nararamdaman ang lamig at tamis. Ang pulp sa gitna ay may nerve at dugo. Iyon ang inaalagaan ng root canal. Tinatakpan ng cementum ang ugat. Kapag magasgas o natunaw ang enamel, hindi na tumutubo ang bagong layer, kaya importante ang acid, pagkiskis, at malakas na kuskos.',
    chipsEn: ['What is a cavity?', 'Why are my teeth sensitive?'],
    chipsTl: ['Ano ang cavity?', 'Bakit maselan ang ngipin ko?'],
