    keys: ['sealant', 'sealants', 'groove', 'molar'],
    en: 'A sealant is a thin coating painted into the grooves of a back tooth, usually for children and teens. It keeps food and bacteria out of pits that a brush misses. It does not treat a cavity that is already there. The tooth has to be checked first. It is quick and does not need numbing.',
    tl: 'Ang sealant ay manipis na coating sa uka ng bagang, madalas para sa bata at teenager. Pinipigilan nito ang pagkain at bacteria sa hukay na hindi naaabot ng sipilyo. Hindi nito ginagamot ang cavity na nandoon na. Kailangang tingnan muna ang ngipin. Mabilis ito at hindi kailangan ng pampamanhid.',
